2026-08-25T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-1146) 'The latent-to-Pixal3D loop
 # uuid: db2249b5-bfe2-54e0-ad92-b70280817b08
 # tags: rfd:title, rfd:flight-level:l1, rfd:attest-in:none
 RFD:Published  1 RFD
 Serials:Weftspun

2026-08-25T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-1146) 'loop 4 of the four-loop plan
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD1146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-1146) '`fourloops-plan.usda`
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD1146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-1146) 'Loop 4 leaves the image plane, and its router waits on calibration.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD1146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-1146) 'The router decides which repair arm runs, and it decides on a statistic nobody has calibrated.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD1146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-1146) 'Read RFD66606-1143 next, the first of the other three loops.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD1146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-1146) 'Build it, and treat the router as uncalibrated until measured.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-1146) 'The statistic is spread over mean, and a spread above 0.15 selects the latent arm. `routerCalibrated` is 0 in the plan, so that threshold is a starting value rather than a result. A router that picks the wrong arm produces a repair that cannot help, and the loop still terminates.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-1146) '**The hazard is an arm that cannot take what the loop holds.** VoxHammer raises `NotImplementedError` outside stub mode, and it takes a mesh where the loop carries a latent. So the arm passes through `/extract` first, and a route that skips that step fails inside the tool rather than at the boundary.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-1146) 'RFD66606-1143, RFD66606-1144 and RFD66606-1145 are the other three loops. RFD66606-1122 is the goal, and RFD66606-1132 lists what converts.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD1146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-1146) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-1146) 'Loop 4 is the only one that leaves the image plane. Pixal3D proposes a latent state, then views, then a glb; EditScore scores; and the repair arm forks between VoxHammer and OmniGen2. At size XL it is the largest of the four, and it is the only loop with a router.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1146  1 LINE
 Text:Written
